            {
              "kind": "markdown",
              "text": "This repo is a local usage-analytics project for GitHub Copilot, not a web app.\n\n- Purpose: collect Copilot usage from VS Code and Copilot CLI logs, normalize them, and generate readable JSON/tree reports.\n- Main parts:\n  - collectors/common.py: shared logic for tickets, credit math, aggregation, and output rendering.\n  - collectors/vscode/: reads VS Code chat/session logs from the user data directory and reports usage by ticket/workspace/model.\n  - collectors/copilot_cli/: reads Copilot CLI session logs from ~/.copilot and emits the same schema for comparison.\n  - reports/: generated output snapshots such as copilot-cli.json and vscode-copilot.json.\n- What the reports include:\n  - session/request totals\n  - AI credits and tokens\n  - ticket attribution (e.g. LEGO-123)\n  - workspace/model breakdown\n  - quota/accounting info\n- In short: it’s a Python-based dashboard/collector for Copilot billing and usage auditing."
            }
