              "kind": "markdown",
              "text": "This repository is a **local GitHub Copilot usage reporting toolkit**, not a web dashboard. It has three Python collectors that read usage data stored on your machine and emit JSON reports or a readable tree. They use only the Python standard library and make no network calls.\n\n- `collectors/vscode/` reads VS Code Copilot Chat session storage.\n- `collectors/copilot_cli/` reads Copilot CLI event logs.\n- `collectors/intellij/` combines JetBrains AI Assistant chat history with linked Copilot CLI usage logs.\n- `collectors/common.py` provides shared config handling, ticket detection, credit rounding, totals, and output formatting.\n- `reports/` contains example/generated reports.\n\nThe collectors normalize their results into a common session/request/tool-call-round schema, with totals by ticket, workspace, and model. They can also report tokens, credits, and—where available—quota data. Ticket detection defaults to the `LEGO-123` pattern and can be configured.\n\nFor example, run `python3 collectors/vscode/collect.py --format tree` to print a readable report, or use `--out reports/vscode-copilot.json` to write JSON. Each collector has a README with its data locations, configuration, and options.\n\nThe worktree currently has uncommitted changes, including changes to the Copilot CLI collector and reports, plus new IntelliJ collector files."
